# How the code in controllib/ is written, for clang-format (checked with clang-format 19).
#
# For new and changed lines only. Do not run clang-format over a whole file here: about 16 % of the existing lines
# would change (2026-11; most of them are ControlLib.c's declarations of Intel's structures, which have several
# members on a line).
#
# 4 spaces. Every brace on its own line; a short if or loop may stay on one line. "Type* name". At most 120 columns.
# { 1, 2 } with spaces inside. The values of #defines that follow each other are aligned in a column. Comments are
# wrapped by hand, and the includes stay in the order they are in.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 120
PointerAlignment: Left
BreakBeforeBraces: Allman
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: WithoutElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
Cpp11BracedListStyle: false
AlignConsecutiveMacros: Consecutive
ReflowComments: false
SortIncludes: false
